@page "/AccessibilityStatement"
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Accessibility statement";
    ViewData["PageTitle"] = "Accessibility statement";
}

<p class="govuk-body">
    This accessibility statement applies to the Histopathology System. It is run by the Animal and Plant Health
    Agency (APHA), an executive agency of the Department for Environment, Food and Rural Affairs (Defra).
    We want as many people as possible to be able to use this service.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">How you should be able to use this service</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">You should be able to:</p>
<ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>change colours, contrast levels and fonts using browser settings or plugins</li>
    <li>zoom in up to 400% without the text spilling off the screen</li>
    <li>navigate the service using just a keyboard</li>
    <li>navigate the service using speech recognition software</li>
    <li>listen to the service using a screen reader</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Compliance status</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">
    This service is fully compliant with the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) version 2.2 AA standard.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Non-accessible content</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">
    We are not aware of any content in this service that does not meet the WCAG 2.2 AA standard.
    An independent accessibility review identified a number of issues. These have all been fixed, and a Defra
    Senior Accessibility Consultant has confirmed following a follow-up check that they have been resolved.
    If you find a problem that is not listed here, please tell us using the contact details below.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Feedback and contact information</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">
    If you need information in a different format, or if you find a problem with the service, please email
    <a class="govuk-link" href="mailto:itu.helpdesk@apha.gov.uk">itu.helpdesk@apha.gov.uk</a>.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Enforcement procedure</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">
    If you are not satisfied with our response, you can contact the Equality Advisory and Support Service
    (EASS) or the Equality Commission for Northern Ireland (ECNI) as appropriate.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">What we are doing to improve accessibility</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">
    We will keep this statement up to date for the life of the service. We review it each time the service
    changes and at least once every 12 months, and will update it if new accessibility issues are found.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">How we tested this service</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">
    The service was reviewed by Defra accessibility specialists. The issues identified were fixed and the fixes
    were confirmed by a Defra Senior Accessibility Consultant. We also test pages for keyboard access, focus
    styles, reading order, colour contrast, form labels and responsive behaviour.
</p>

<p class="govuk-body">
    This statement was last reviewed on 10 November 2026.
</p>
